{
  "id": "COMPOUND:40032 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential pathway by which 30-Oxopseudotaraxasterol may interact with the High-affinity choline transporter. This is supported by the shared relationship between 30-Oxopseudotaraxasterol and ZR-75-1, which is the target of multiple compounds, including Armepavine and romidepsin, both of which have a known target of the High-affinity choline transporter. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same downstream pathway indicates a possible mechanism of action involving the choline transporter. The integration of these findings suggests that 30-Oxopseudotaraxasterol may act through a common intermediate, ZR-75-1, to influence the choline transporter, potentially through a shared biochemical mechanism. The evidence supports a role for 30-Oxopseudotaraxasterol in modulating the choline transporter, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
